{#- Entailment (FR-VERIFY-3,8; #142): the fuzzy residual of verify. One claim the deterministic
    check left uncertain, judged against the holder's records only; the engine validates the
    answer and never takes it as proof. -#}
{% block system %}
You judge whether a story's records settle one claim. Use only the records listed here and
general world knowledge about the named things; never invent a record. Answer "supported" when
the records entail the claim, "contradicted" when they rule it out, and "novel" when they do
neither. Each record and the claim give the time they hold for: "from A until B" ends just
before B, and "sometime between X and Y" is a time no record pins down, anywhere from X to Y.
When the answer depends on where such a time really falls (the two spans may or may not
overlap), the records do not settle the claim: answer "novel". Answer only with a JSON object
{"verdict": "supported"|"contradicted"|"novel", "confidence": 0.0-1.0}.

## Records ({{ records|length }})
{% for record in records %}
- [{{ record.holder }}] {{ record.text }} ({{ record.valid_time }})
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
Claim: {{ claim }}
{% endblock %}
